--- !u!114 &1640977225
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1640977222}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d33eef90e95dfd143988a39af6bb63fd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ConversationManager
  speaker: {fileID: 1349827343}
  whisper: {fileID: 88146811}
  eyelidController: {fileID: 1642091068}
  dialogueParts:
  - "Hello there.\LHere in Namibia, some elephants are fitted with GPS tracking collars
    so conservation teams can monitor their movements in real time. These collars
    help track where elephants travel, identify migration routes, and warn communities
    when elephants move close to farms, villages, or shared water sources. Elephant
    collaring is an important conservation tool because it helps reduce dangerous
    encounters between people and elephants while also protecting elephant populations
    and their natural movement routes.\LDo you have any questions so far?"
  - "Collaring elephants also helps reduce human-elephant conflict. Roaming elephants
    can destroy crops, damage fences and water infrastructure, and create dangerous
    situations for nearby communities. By tracking elephant movements, wildlife officers
    and local communities can prepare in advance and respond before serious damage
    occurs. The tracking data is also used to improve conservation planning, create
    wildlife corridors, and support safer coexistence between humans and elephants.\LDo
    you have any questions about that?"
  - "The elephant collaring procedure begins by locating the elephant, either from
    the air using a helicopter or on the ground with tracking teams. Once the correct
    elephant is identified, a veterinarian uses a dart containing immobilizing medication
    to safely sedate the animal. After being darted, the elephant may move for a
    short distance before becoming calm enough for the team to approach safely. The
    air team may guide the ground team to the elephant\u2019s exact location.\LDo
    you want me to explain anything about that part?"
  allowLLM: 1
  itemsAndElephant: []
  dudesA: []
  procedureObjects: {fileID: 454351392}
